  "narration": [
    {
      "id": "vo1",
      "start": 0.12,
      "text": "He didn't open the door.",
      "caption": "HE DIDN'T OPEN THE DOOR."
    },
    {
      "id": "vo2",
      "start": 2.15,
      "text": "The window was enough.",
      "caption": "THE WINDOW WAS ENOUGH."
    },
    {
      "id": "vo3",
      "start": 4.35,
      "text": "But why climb into a stranger's car?",
      "caption": "WHY CLIMB INTO A STRANGER'S CAR?"
    },
    {
      "id": "vo4",
      "start": 7.25,
      "text": "Not for a ride. For whatever food he can find.",
      "caption": "NOT FOR A RIDE. FOR FOOD HE CAN FIND."
    },
    {
      "id": "vo5",
      "start": 11.35,
      "text": "If one search ends with food, the lesson can stick.",
      "caption": "IF A SEARCH ENDS WITH FOOD, THE LESSON CAN STICK."
    },
    {
      "id": "vo6",
      "start": 16.25,
      "text": "Search. Reward. Repeat.",
      "caption": "SEARCH. REWARD. REPEAT."
    },
    {
      "id": "vo7",
      "start": 19.35,
      "text": "That's food conditioning: a car becomes a place worth checking again.",
      "caption": "FOOD CONDITIONING MAKES A CAR WORTH CHECKING AGAIN."
    },
    {
      "id": "vo8",
      "start": 25.2,
      "text": "Even when nothing is visible, the learned shortcut can remain.",
      "caption": "EVEN WHEN NOTHING IS VISIBLE, THE SHORTCUT CAN REMAIN."
    },
    {
      "id": "vo9",
      "start": 30.35,
      "text": "So don't teach the lesson. Secure food and lock up.",
      "caption": "DON'T TEACH THE LESSON. SECURE FOOD AND LOCK UP."
    }
  ],
